<title>SWITZERLAND: CYCLING-BOARDMAN WINS TOUR DE ROMANDIE TIME TRIAL.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-BOARDMAN WINS TOUR DE ROMANDIE TIME TRIAL.</headline>
<dateline>KRIEGSTETTEN, Switzerland 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings</p>
<p>of the 8.1-km Tour de Romandie time trial prologue on Tuesday:</p>
<p>1. Chris Boardman (Britain) nine minutes 58.06 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Erik Breukink (Netherlands)     2.26 seconds behind</p>
<p> 3. Dariusz Baranowski (Poland)     3.87</p>
<p> 4. Paolo Savoldelli (Italy)	  4.13</p>
<p> 5. Johan Bruyneel (Belgium)	  6.28</p>
<p> 6. Erik Dekker (Netherlands)	 8.96</p>
<p>7. Peter Meinert-Nielsen (Denmark) 9.25</p>
<p> 8. Viatcheslav Ekimov (Russia)    14.09</p>
<p> 9. Beat Zberg (Switzerland)	 15.75</p>
<p>10. Bruno Boscardin (Switzerland) 15.93</p>
<p> 11. Angelo Lecchi (Italy)	   15.97</p>
<p> 12. Michael Blaudzun (Denmark)    15.98</p>
<p> 13. Michele Colombo (Italy)	 16.09</p>
<p> 14. Tony Rominger (Switzerland)   17.61</p>
<p> 15. Fabiano Fontanelli (Italy)    17.90</p>
